        "id": 16465
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-20T13:49:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AFAIK, any project used to act like an admin project. So it didn\u0027t matter which project you had the admin role on, as long as you had it. This does the same thing by returning True by default.",
      "parentUuid": "7a8ec9b2_b3b90731",
      "revId": "b78d9cfc463f21516dc0be055dc4e0428c37c637",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a8ec9b2_494c7970",
        "filename": "keystone/models/token_model.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 235,
      "author": {
        "id": 7191
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-09-20T22:50:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, when admin_project is not defined as in older versions of keystone every project was an admin project. So we default to true to say yes this is an admin project so it doesn\u0027t fail new policies.",
      "parentUuid": "7a8ec9b2_7354df53",
      "revId": "b78d9cfc463f21516dc0be055dc4e0428c37c637",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3a98d1f4_71beda00",
        "filename": "keystone/models/token_model.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 235,
